{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01418",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.12,
      "end_seconds": 3.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Afternoon, thanks for coming in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.43,
      "end_seconds": 9.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.49,
      "end_seconds": 16.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.97,
      "end_seconds": 22.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "absolutely, come and and sit beside them how are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 24.48,
      "end_seconds": 33.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "um, it's a red warm patch on my shin, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.65,
      "end_seconds": 39.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "okay, what do you take on a a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.47,
      "end_seconds": 43.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "I take carbamazepine, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.89,
      "end_seconds": 47.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Okay, how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.69,
      "end_seconds": 59.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "200 milligrams. It's metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.65,
      "end_seconds": 80.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.94,
      "end_seconds": 87.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.06,
      "end_seconds": 91.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.63,
      "end_seconds": 113.05,
      "duration_seconds": 19.42,
      "text": "It usually comes with a sore leg. The sore leg? That's been for two weeks. With sore leg, pretty severe, if I'm being honest. I notice it more with walking. I was feeling shivery at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.2,
      "end_seconds": 120.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Any sign of rash elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.22,
      "end_seconds": 124.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Nope, no rash elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 128.85,
      "end_seconds": 134.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice rash elsewhere. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.23,
      "end_seconds": 145.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.89,
      "end_seconds": 154.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any cut or shortness of breath at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.53,
      "end_seconds": 157.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.92,
      "end_seconds": 166.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.78,
      "end_seconds": 168.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "no changes there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.26,
      "end_seconds": 172.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Alright, any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.92,
      "end_seconds": 174.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.31,
      "end_seconds": 179.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.76,
      "end_seconds": 183.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.94,
      "end_seconds": 188.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.95,
      "end_seconds": 194.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Actually, my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis. My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.64,
      "end_seconds": 200.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.11,
      "end_seconds": 207.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Epilepsy, for nearly five years. I have diabetes. I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.61,
      "end_seconds": 208.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.22,
      "end_seconds": 218.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "okay, I can see heart disease in your file as well have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.31,
      "end_seconds": 229.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.37,
      "end_seconds": 234.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.57,
      "end_seconds": 250.3,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I quit smoking around ten years ago. I swim twice a week. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 265.96,
      "end_seconds": 278.15,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Heart rate 95, respiratory rate 16. Saturation 97 percent, BP is 104 over 68, temperature is 38.1 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.3,
      "end_seconds": 280.0,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.28,
      "end_seconds": 286.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.99,
      "end_seconds": 290.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.17,
      "end_seconds": 308.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "the shin is red, warm and tender with a clear edge, and I've marked it it with a pen"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.28,
      "end_seconds": 309.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.69,
      "end_seconds": 317.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.9,
      "end_seconds": 337.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I don't have a clear answer today: cellulitis of the leg is possible, and so is a blood clot in the leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.85,
      "end_seconds": 341.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.97,
      "end_seconds": 356.22,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now cellulitis of the leg is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange blood tests for cellulitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.91,
      "end_seconds": 362.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "um, that's fine with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.71,
      "end_seconds": 381.88,
      "duration_seconds": 19.17,
      "text": "You'll be taking flucloxacillin, 500 milligrams, four times a day, seven days. That should help with cellulitis. Keep the leg raised and come back if the redness goes past the pen line. See me again in two days. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.94,
      "end_seconds": 386.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.46,
      "end_seconds": 388.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}